WEBVTT

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:40.413
Whoa...

00:00:40.414 --> 00:00:43.127
- It's a box fit for a king, it is.

00:00:43.128 --> 00:00:44.296
- As it should be.

00:00:44.297 --> 00:00:47.218
We are delivering it to
the King of Space himself.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:48.638
- A real-life king?

00:00:48.639 --> 00:00:51.018
This could be my big chance to grovel!

00:00:58.576 --> 00:01:00.788
Ooh. Swanky dump.

00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:03.920
- Your delivery, my liege.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.511
- Now, this guy knows how to grovel.

00:01:08.512 --> 00:01:10.599
- Yes!
- At last.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.270
The portrait of
my late wife has arrived.

00:01:13.271 --> 00:01:15.149
Careful! It's delicate!

00:01:18.281 --> 00:01:21.370
Infinita, Queen of Space.

00:01:21.371 --> 00:01:24.919
Not even the finest macaroni artist
could capture your beauty.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.380
Although this one did.

00:01:26.381 --> 00:01:27.634
Hang it over there!

00:01:32.393 --> 00:01:35.147
- Sorry. It's my early-onset sciatica.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.239
- Announcing His Royal Highness,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.243
the Prince of Space!

00:01:41.244 --> 00:01:44.250
- Allow me to help your elderly friend.

00:01:49.987 --> 00:01:52.408
Wow. This absolute stud

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:54.912
sure made me look like a wimp, Leela?

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:57.083
You guys straighten that together
while I explain

00:01:57.084 --> 00:02:00.256
our loyalty punch card program
to His Majesty.

00:02:03.764 --> 00:02:05.684
- I still don't understand.

00:02:05.685 --> 00:02:08.398
Ten punches, and I get 10% off?

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:10.486
- No, no. It's nothing like that.

00:02:10.487 --> 00:02:13.575
Let N be the number of punches.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.502
Leela, where were you?
It's been, like, 30 minutes.

00:02:18.503 --> 00:02:20.923
- I was falling in love
with the Prince of Space.

00:02:20.924 --> 00:02:22.133
We're getting married!

00:02:24.973 --> 00:02:27.353
I know this is very sudden, Fry.

00:02:27.354 --> 00:02:29.732
I'll always remember the times we had

00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:31.528
that I haven't already forgotten.

00:02:31.529 --> 00:02:33.823
- But, but, I love you!

00:02:33.824 --> 00:02:35.953
And I can't afford to live without you!

00:02:38.976 --> 00:02:41.188
Futurama is brought to you by...

00:02:41.189 --> 00:02:44.235
Windos! The toy so fun,

00:02:44.236 --> 00:02:46.239
it makes fun look like boredom!

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:02.673
- Good news, Windos!

00:03:04.386 --> 00:03:08.101
Today, we're delivering sushi
to Mrs. McDougal.

00:03:10.105 --> 00:03:12.484
- Another job well done.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.786
- Are you okay, Fry?

00:03:17.787 --> 00:03:20.082
I'm just a little run down.

00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:22.211
- Run down? I'm sure it's nothing,

00:03:22.212 --> 00:03:23.673
but you should see a doctor.

00:03:23.674 --> 00:03:26.178
- Run down? I'm sure it's nothing,

00:03:26.179 --> 00:03:27.848
but you should see a doctor.

00:03:27.849 --> 00:03:30.772
Me! Right. Let's take a listen.

00:03:32.943 --> 00:03:34.779
Dear God, no!

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.702
Pretend you didn't hear that.

00:03:38.746 --> 00:03:40.457
- Are you sure, Dr. Zoidberg?

00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:42.293
I mean, you're usually wrong.

00:03:42.294 --> 00:03:43.630
- Of course, I'm sure.

00:03:43.631 --> 00:03:46.636
Fry's mainspring is nearly wound down.

00:03:47.973 --> 00:03:49.266
Dear.

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.894
It must have been all that time

00:03:50.895 --> 00:03:53.733
Fry spent cryogenically frozen.

00:03:54.945 --> 00:03:56.531
For a thousand years,

00:03:56.532 --> 00:03:59.954
he was slowly pacing and winding down.

00:04:05.048 --> 00:04:08.972
- Welcome to the world of Windos!

00:04:08.973 --> 00:04:11.519
- It was a one-way ticket to Oldsville!

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.150
Last exit before Deathburg!

00:04:15.403 --> 00:04:18.282
I'm so sorry, Fry.

00:04:18.283 --> 00:04:19.785
We'll take it day-by-day.

00:04:19.786 --> 00:04:21.623
- I'd suggest minute-by-minute.

00:04:21.624 --> 00:04:23.250
Well, don't be sad.

00:04:23.251 --> 00:04:25.129
I've had a full life.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.426
I eated. I prayed.

00:04:27.427 --> 00:04:28.970
I loved-ed.

00:04:28.971 --> 00:04:30.599
I'm at peace.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.853
- At peace? At peace?!

00:04:32.854 --> 00:04:34.690
You selfish jerk!

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:36.361
You're my best friend!

00:04:36.362 --> 00:04:38.238
Promise you won't leave me!

00:04:38.239 --> 00:04:40.076
- I can't help winding down.

00:04:40.077 --> 00:04:41.496
- That's crazy talk!

00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:43.708
You need spiritual guidance!

00:04:48.703 --> 00:04:50.372
You gotta help him, Reverend.

00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:54.297
Do you have any way to calm
my friend's terror of mortality?

00:04:54.298 --> 00:04:57.595
- Can religion calm
the terror of mortality?

00:04:57.596 --> 00:04:59.640
That's our home run swing!

00:04:59.641 --> 00:05:02.730
After you wind down, you rise up!

00:05:02.731 --> 00:05:06.404
You spread your wings
and fly around Heaven forever,

00:05:06.405 --> 00:05:08.073
as an angel.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:09.744
Really?

00:05:09.745 --> 00:05:11.748
A-And we can do loop-de-loops?

00:05:11.749 --> 00:05:12.875
- Well, no, not...

00:05:12.876 --> 00:05:14.962
Loop-de-loops, you say?

00:05:14.963 --> 00:05:17.551
Well, maybe Fry can face death after all.

00:05:17.552 --> 00:05:18.970
- Bender, my son.

00:05:18.971 --> 00:05:22.436
Heaven's not a actual place
the way Hell is.

00:05:22.437 --> 00:05:25.567
It's a metaphor for how the soul lives on

00:05:25.568 --> 00:05:28.531
in the hearts of those who love us.

00:05:28.532 --> 00:05:32.498
- Metaphor? Isn't that just
a fancy word for "steaming load"?

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:34.335
- I wouldn't call it fancy.

00:05:34.336 --> 00:05:38.260
Preacherbot gave me nothing!

00:05:38.261 --> 00:05:39.845
Can no one help me?

00:05:39.846 --> 00:05:42.225
- Well, some say
there's a guru high in the...

00:05:42.226 --> 00:05:45.022
Some say it? Let's go!

00:05:55.712 --> 00:05:57.715
I can't go much further.

00:05:57.716 --> 00:05:59.719
Escaping from that wind-up Yeti

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.056
used most of my remaining power.

00:06:03.811 --> 00:06:05.522
Fry!

00:06:05.523 --> 00:06:07.150
- Goodbye, friends.

00:06:07.151 --> 00:06:08.903
Maybe we'll meet again

00:06:08.904 --> 00:06:10.907
in a better metaphor.

00:06:18.341 --> 00:06:21.011
- Bender, he's gone. It's over.

00:06:21.012 --> 00:06:23.015
- Never! I'm gonna give him

00:06:23.016 --> 00:06:25.355
spring-to-spring resuscitation!

00:06:36.418 --> 00:06:39.298
- Wha... What happened? Am I alive?

00:06:39.299 --> 00:06:42.721
- If you were dead, how could
you ask such a dumb question?

00:06:42.722 --> 00:06:45.142
You're as alive and stupid as ever.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.900
- You saved him, Bender!

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:50.236
You're a hero!

00:06:50.237 --> 00:06:52.449
Shut up, baby, I know it.

00:06:53.661 --> 00:06:55.162
- Are you okay, robot?

00:06:55.163 --> 00:06:56.916
Never better!

00:06:56.917 --> 00:06:59.296
Wound up tight and full of

00:06:59.297 --> 00:07:01.593
spring...

00:07:02.303 --> 00:07:05.267
Goodbye, sweet jerks.

00:07:07.439 --> 00:07:09.275
- Bender! No!

00:07:17.505 --> 00:07:19.760
- Now, that's dead.

00:07:28.129 --> 00:07:31.552
- Bender saved my life, and now he's gone.

00:07:31.553 --> 00:07:33.264
What does it all mean?

00:07:33.265 --> 00:07:35.769
- It means life is meaningless.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.564
Lesson learned! Let's hit the road.

00:07:37.565 --> 00:07:39.402
- No! I need answers!

00:07:39.403 --> 00:07:41.155
I'm continuing up to that guru,

00:07:41.156 --> 00:07:43.075
no matter how long the journey.

00:07:44.204 --> 00:07:46.165
Are you the guru of the mountain?

00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:48.169
- For a quarter, I'm a guru.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:51.343
For a nickel, you get a sticker that says
you climbed the mountain.

00:07:51.802 --> 00:07:54.640
- My friend wound down
and fell in a volcano.

00:07:54.641 --> 00:07:57.563
Is that the end? Just nothingness?

00:07:57.564 --> 00:07:58.648
I found a quarter.

00:08:03.659 --> 00:08:06.706
- Take solace,
for the spirit of your friend

00:08:06.707 --> 00:08:08.168
is eternal.

00:08:08.169 --> 00:08:10.839
It will be reincarnated in other bodies,

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.678
growing and learning as it goes...

00:08:13.679 --> 00:08:15.098
Some say.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.603
- Reincarnation?

00:08:17.604 --> 00:08:19.982
That sounds like another
big, steaming load.

00:08:19.983 --> 00:08:22.028
- Load? Perhaps.

00:08:22.029 --> 00:08:24.618
Steaming? Perhaps not.

00:08:26.455 --> 00:08:28.208
Look!

00:08:28.209 --> 00:08:30.796
- I'm back, baby!
And I'm doing loop-de-loops!

00:08:30.797 --> 00:08:33.176
Woo!

00:08:33.177 --> 00:08:35.347
Woo!

00:08:37.477 --> 00:08:39.730
- Maybe, in some weird way,

00:08:39.731 --> 00:08:41.651
the soul really is eternal.

00:08:41.652 --> 00:08:44.782
- Bite my enlightened
metal ass, mortality!

00:08:44.783 --> 00:08:46.828
I'm 40% aerodynamic!

00:08:46.829 --> 00:08:48.540
That's not aerodynamic enough!

00:08:53.926 --> 00:08:56.931
- It's fine.
- He'll be something else in a minute.

00:08:56.932 --> 00:08:58.643
Collect all 293.

00:08:58.644 --> 00:09:01.190
And now, back to our program.

00:09:04.197 --> 00:09:06.159
- Marriage? I forbid it!

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.912
She is a space commoner!

00:09:08.497 --> 00:09:11.794
- That was a close one.
- Let's head home, honey.

00:09:14.242 --> 00:09:17.206
No. No one is
head-home-honey-ing anywhere.

00:09:17.207 --> 00:09:19.168
- What? Why?

00:09:19.169 --> 00:09:20.545
- What?
- Why?!

00:09:20.546 --> 00:09:22.841
- Because Leela's not common.

00:09:22.842 --> 00:09:25.222
She's brave and good and articulate.

00:09:25.223 --> 00:09:26.058
- Blah?

00:09:26.059 --> 00:09:29.188
- How can you stand in the way
of true love, Your Majesty?

00:09:29.189 --> 00:09:32.444
Space Queen Infinita
would be ashamed of you.

00:09:34.616 --> 00:09:36.786
- How dare you!

00:09:36.787 --> 00:09:40.294
- I've never been so angry and hungry.

00:09:42.257 --> 00:09:43.967
She needs salt.

00:09:43.968 --> 00:09:46.306
- My wife needs no seasoning!

00:09:46.307 --> 00:09:48.268
I challenge you to a duel!

00:09:48.269 --> 00:09:51.858
- I accept.
And if I win, the wedding is on.

00:09:51.859 --> 00:09:55.449
- And if I win, your head is off!

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.373
Futurama is brought to you by...

00:09:59.374 --> 00:10:00.792
Round Wheels!

00:10:00.793 --> 00:10:02.921
The only toy car with wheels.

00:10:23.197 --> 00:10:25.242
- Good news, Round Wheels!

00:10:25.243 --> 00:10:29.083
We're delivering a piece of
replacement track to Saturn.

00:10:30.628 --> 00:10:33.466
And everybody is going. All of us!

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:35.137
- Yay!

00:10:35.138 --> 00:10:39.103
- Except one, since only six
can fit in the shipmobile.

00:10:39.104 --> 00:10:41.608
- Well, I stayed behind last time, so...

00:10:41.609 --> 00:10:42.943
- I suggest Zoidberg.

00:10:42.944 --> 00:10:45.617
Second!

00:11:01.732 --> 00:11:03.360
- Should we test it out?

00:11:19.393 --> 00:11:22.022
- Why doesn't anybody like me?

00:11:22.023 --> 00:11:24.694
- You're depressed, you're depressing,

00:11:24.695 --> 00:11:27.324
and you talk while
we're trying to watch TV!

00:11:27.325 --> 00:11:29.912
- The high-speed chase
finally came to an end

00:11:29.913 --> 00:11:31.833
when friction caused the cars

00:11:31.834 --> 00:11:34.630
to gradually slow down. Morbo?

00:11:34.631 --> 00:11:37.469
- In local news,
countless victims have died

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:40.851
after viewing a mysterious video
circulating online.

00:11:40.852 --> 00:11:42.981
- Let's see some of that video.

00:11:48.868 --> 00:11:50.579
- The video is invariably followed

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:53.084
by an equally mysterious phone call.

00:11:53.085 --> 00:11:55.339
Scientists say
anyone who answers the call

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:57.634
will die tragically within hours.

00:11:58.721 --> 00:12:00.807
- Can you pause it?
I'm getting a call.

00:12:00.808 --> 00:12:02.186
- No!
- Amy, stop!

00:12:02.187 --> 00:12:03.563
Hello?

00:12:03.564 --> 00:12:05.985
Your car warranty has expired.

00:12:05.986 --> 00:12:09.367
Press one now,
whether or not you want to renew.

00:12:20.098 --> 00:12:22.893
- Yes, I'm here to pick up
my extended warranty.

00:12:22.894 --> 00:12:24.356
I have a 3:00 AM appointment.

00:12:37.566 --> 00:12:39.735
- Have you seen Amy
since that creepy video

00:12:39.736 --> 00:12:41.322
and chilling phone call?

00:12:41.323 --> 00:12:43.076
No, but my phone's ringing.

00:12:43.077 --> 00:12:44.537
Maybe it's her.

00:12:44.538 --> 00:12:46.125
Yello? What?

00:12:46.584 --> 00:12:48.587
I don't recognize the chilling voice.

00:12:48.588 --> 00:12:50.424
Put it on speakerphone.

00:12:50.425 --> 00:12:54.056
Am sorry to inform you
your car warranty has expired.

00:12:54.057 --> 00:12:57.479
- We don't want any!
What do they think, we're idiots?

00:13:06.833 --> 00:13:10.339
- Some ancient horror
is picking us off one by one,

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.217
starting with the most gullible.

00:13:12.218 --> 00:13:14.472
Who will be next?

00:13:14.473 --> 00:13:17.102
- Hermes, quit frightening me
while I'm on the phone.

00:13:20.903 --> 00:13:22.488
- Goodbye, robot!

00:13:22.489 --> 00:13:24.492
- Wait! I have a desperate idea!

00:13:24.493 --> 00:13:26.746
We'll race after Bender,
and let him lead us

00:13:26.747 --> 00:13:28.750
to the monster's den of terror!

00:13:28.751 --> 00:13:32.174
- Hurray! Road trip to the monster's den!

00:13:32.175 --> 00:13:33.677
- Except you, Zoidberg.

00:13:33.678 --> 00:13:35.974
Someone has to stay behind
to answer the phones.

00:13:42.529 --> 00:13:44.950
- Come on!
We'll pick up speed on the downhill

00:13:44.951 --> 00:13:46.912
since we have no motors!

00:13:50.946 --> 00:13:53.533
Woo! I'm doing loop-de-loops!

00:13:53.534 --> 00:13:56.080
I'm not gonna make it!

00:13:56.081 --> 00:13:57.625
Go on without me!

00:13:57.626 --> 00:13:59.086
- That was my plan.

00:14:01.383 --> 00:14:02.720
- I'm okay!

00:14:06.811 --> 00:14:08.481
- Yes, I'm here for the free scam.

00:14:15.286 --> 00:14:18.668
I'll have to drop it
and limbo under that arm.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.980
Sweet Subaru of Timbuktu!

00:14:28.981 --> 00:14:31.192
It's a chop shop.

00:14:32.404 --> 00:14:33.864
Wh-Who are you?

00:14:35.451 --> 00:14:38.081
- It's me, Zoidberg.

00:14:38.082 --> 00:14:41.004
- Thank goodness.
- I was afraid it was the villain.

00:14:41.005 --> 00:14:42.256
- I am the villain!

00:14:42.257 --> 00:14:45.972
- No. Villains have more charisma.
You're just boring.

00:14:45.973 --> 00:14:48.268
- No one ever included me.

00:14:48.269 --> 00:14:50.898
So, I included all of you, why not?

00:14:50.899 --> 00:14:53.863
Now, I have Fry's roof rack, Amy's bumper,

00:14:53.864 --> 00:14:55.282
and, spoiler alert,

00:14:55.283 --> 00:14:56.910
Leela's spoiler!

00:14:56.911 --> 00:14:58.538
Help, we're trapped!

00:14:58.539 --> 00:15:00.584
Inside Zoidberg!

00:15:00.585 --> 00:15:02.671
I'm the gas tank, by the way.

00:15:02.672 --> 00:15:05.552
- And here's my latest acquisition.

00:15:05.553 --> 00:15:07.932
Bender's shiny metal muffler!

00:15:10.814 --> 00:15:13.485
Bite my shiny metal... Forget it.

00:15:13.486 --> 00:15:16.784
- Now, I just need a piece of you, Hermes,

00:15:16.785 --> 00:15:19.413
and we'll all be friends together.

00:15:19.414 --> 00:15:21.000
Forever!

00:15:21.001 --> 00:15:22.002
- Woo! Woo!

00:15:22.003 --> 00:15:23.881
I don't need my oil changed!

00:15:25.661 --> 00:15:29.208
Snap in Hermes' hood, and... done!

00:15:29.209 --> 00:15:31.421
I'll never be alone again!

00:15:31.422 --> 00:15:32.674
Oop! Oop, hang on.

00:15:32.675 --> 00:15:34.678
I accidentally took off my mouth.

00:15:34.679 --> 00:15:36.264
Let me just put that back onto...

00:15:37.894 --> 00:15:41.065
Let's hit the track, people!

00:15:49.333 --> 00:15:51.670
Don't worry. I bought the warranty!

00:15:59.186 --> 00:16:01.522
And now, back to our program.

00:16:09.456 --> 00:16:13.171
The duel of the King of Space
versus the Fry of Earth

00:16:13.172 --> 00:16:14.883
shall now commence!

00:16:14.884 --> 00:16:18.306
Competitors, mount your lamassus!

00:16:20.311 --> 00:16:21.355
- Here you go, boy.

00:16:24.111 --> 00:16:26.573
Thanks. That was really good.

00:16:27.158 --> 00:16:30.790
- Space shall run red
with the blood of the commoner.

00:16:30.791 --> 00:16:32.502
Nice earrings, by the way.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:36.384
- I volunteer to fight in Fry's place,

00:16:36.385 --> 00:16:37.887
as his champion!

00:16:39.266 --> 00:16:42.772
- The rule book does allow for a champion!

00:16:42.773 --> 00:16:45.820
This isn't the rule book, by the way.
It's a takeout menu.

00:16:45.821 --> 00:16:47.156
I'm gonna have the pad Thai.

00:16:47.157 --> 00:16:50.537
- You can't fight for me, Leela.
I'm fighting for you!

00:16:50.538 --> 00:16:53.418
- Fry, you're really bad at fighting.

00:16:53.419 --> 00:16:54.588
- That's true.

00:17:06.946 --> 00:17:09.993
Let the duel commence!

00:17:12.708 --> 00:17:13.919
- Roar.

00:17:16.048 --> 00:17:17.549
- I can't look!

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:18.803
Now I can.

00:17:28.014 --> 00:17:31.812
- The king smells dead!
Long live the king!

00:17:31.813 --> 00:17:33.315
- Yes!

00:17:33.316 --> 00:17:35.945
We can marry at last, my love!

00:17:35.946 --> 00:17:38.618
Sorry about murdering your father.

00:17:39.746 --> 00:17:43.169
- I, too, had a champion fight for me.

00:17:47.803 --> 00:17:49.221
The prince!

00:17:49.222 --> 00:17:52.854
I-I killed my true love!

00:17:52.855 --> 00:17:54.900
- No, I'm fine.
- You mean that guy.

00:18:20.561 --> 00:18:22.439
- Boy, that was a really long delivery.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:24.693
I thought we were gonna fall off
the end of the water.

00:18:24.694 --> 00:18:27.532
- The water doesn't have an end,
numb duck.

00:18:27.533 --> 00:18:29.036
Haven't you ever seen a map?

00:18:30.514 --> 00:18:33.435
- I guess that looks pretty infinite.
- I'm convinced.

00:18:33.436 --> 00:18:35.898
- Well, I'm not! I made this map,

00:18:35.899 --> 00:18:38.863
and whole sections
were based on old legends

00:18:38.864 --> 00:18:40.324
and random hunches.

00:18:40.325 --> 00:18:44.373
I propose a voyage of
scientific exploration!

00:18:44.374 --> 00:18:45.374
- Okay.

00:18:51.973 --> 00:18:55.145
- To the edge of the water!
If there is an edge.

00:18:55.146 --> 00:18:58.694
- And if not, an agonizing death
with friends!

00:18:58.695 --> 00:19:01.784
- Make way for rubber ducklings.

00:19:12.765 --> 00:19:15.853
- Oy, how long have we been at sea?

00:19:15.854 --> 00:19:18.651
- Always!
- And how far have we traveled?

00:19:18.652 --> 00:19:21.072
- With no landmarks, it's hard to say.

00:19:21.073 --> 00:19:23.744
There's a good chance
we never moved at all.

00:19:23.745 --> 00:19:25.749
Fry, check the spyglass.

00:19:31.135 --> 00:19:33.096
- Land ho!

00:19:33.097 --> 00:19:35.392
- What's land?
- I don't know.

00:19:44.152 --> 00:19:45.781
Yep.

00:19:46.783 --> 00:19:49.370
- Father, what is that
unusual piece of land

00:19:49.371 --> 00:19:50.498
floating toward us?

00:19:50.499 --> 00:19:52.752
It be invaders!

00:19:52.753 --> 00:19:55.298
Take shelter in the fun-time beach house!

00:19:55.299 --> 00:19:57.679
- But, I see a stranger,

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:01.019
and his bill looks gentle and kind.

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:07.198
- Look at his eyeballs! It's the scurvy!

00:20:09.202 --> 00:20:12.876
- What strange folk. Do you come in peace?

00:20:12.877 --> 00:20:14.212
- We're still deciding.

00:20:14.672 --> 00:20:17.301
I don't trust these land wobblers.

00:20:17.302 --> 00:20:20.767
Let's just trade our guns for tobacco
and get out of here.

00:20:20.768 --> 00:20:22.979
- Alright, rubber flockers.

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:25.735
Turn around and float back
where you came from!

00:20:25.736 --> 00:20:29.283
- Never!
Peck him until he falls down!

00:20:32.107 --> 00:20:34.653
- Stop! Stop this madness!

00:20:34.654 --> 00:20:37.450
Kind strangers, welcome to our land.

00:20:37.451 --> 00:20:39.663
We call it land.

00:20:39.664 --> 00:20:41.667
- That's so interesting.

00:20:41.668 --> 00:20:43.336
We call our land water.

00:20:43.337 --> 00:20:45.675
- Won't you join us for a turducky dinner?

00:20:45.676 --> 00:20:47.344
- Sure. What's in it?

00:20:50.644 --> 00:20:53.064
- My name's Fry. Is that your name, too?

00:20:53.065 --> 00:20:56.279
- No, I'm Leela. What are you doing?

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:58.199
- Trying to gaze into your eye.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.872
I've never seen anyone like you.

00:21:00.873 --> 00:21:03.461
I saw a fish once, though. It was cool.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:11.560
Fry. I'm falling
head over heels in love with you.

00:21:11.561 --> 00:21:15.192
Except I can't fall,
and I don't have heels.

00:21:18.992 --> 00:21:21.705
- Have you gone land crazy, Fry?

00:21:21.706 --> 00:21:24.795
In our culture,
interspecies love is forbidden!

00:21:24.796 --> 00:21:25.797
Yeah?

00:21:25.798 --> 00:21:29.220
Well, in our culture,
we believe a woman's sexuality

00:21:29.221 --> 00:21:30.682
is her own decision!

00:21:30.683 --> 00:21:32.520
Okay, then.

00:21:34.732 --> 00:21:36.443
- But I, as an individual,

00:21:36.444 --> 00:21:38.364
strongly disagree with that view

00:21:38.365 --> 00:21:39.908
and am deeply offended!

00:21:41.186 --> 00:21:43.941
- This means war!

00:21:43.942 --> 00:21:45.945
- War? Well, we don't have that word,

00:21:45.946 --> 00:21:48.576
but this definitely means peace-fighting!

00:21:48.577 --> 00:21:49.995
- Fry!

00:21:49.996 --> 00:21:51.415
- Leela Fry!

00:21:55.758 --> 00:21:57.761
Whee! Two, three, four.

00:21:57.762 --> 00:21:59.013
Whee! Two, three...

00:22:06.696 --> 00:22:08.240
- Rubber in the hole!

00:22:17.593 --> 00:22:18.595
- That tickles.

00:22:22.353 --> 00:22:25.023
- And thus, with a final wobble,

00:22:25.024 --> 00:22:27.152
I do fall down.

00:22:39.136 --> 00:22:42.934
- This is the end. All is lost.
- No.

00:22:42.935 --> 00:22:44.563
Our love is eternal.

00:22:44.564 --> 00:22:47.736
It'll live on forever, even after it dies.

00:22:47.737 --> 00:22:49.656
- That's so stupid,

00:22:49.657 --> 00:22:52.119
but also sweet. Like you.

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.541
Goodbye.

00:22:54.542 --> 00:22:56.546
Goodbye.

00:23:15.401 --> 00:23:17.946
Eggulons. Collect all 11!

00:23:17.947 --> 00:23:20.743
And now, what's left of Futurama.

00:23:25.044 --> 00:23:27.966
- I'm sorry you killed
the love of your life, Leela.

00:23:27.967 --> 00:23:30.012
It must have been horrible for you,

00:23:30.013 --> 00:23:33.477
the way your laser lance
sliced him up like a watermelon.

00:23:33.478 --> 00:23:35.105
- It's okay, Fry.

00:23:35.106 --> 00:23:38.069
I wasn't really in love with him.
I was under a spell.

00:23:38.070 --> 00:23:40.408
Really? A magic spell?

00:23:40.409 --> 00:23:43.247
- No! A science spell!

00:23:43.248 --> 00:23:45.793
Of course...

00:23:49.719 --> 00:23:53.476
Whee! Woo! Woo-hoo-hoo! Yeah!